+
+[\bf Note (bug fix). The original program computed |umaxscope| and |vmaxscope|
+by the recursions
+$$\hbox{|umaxscope[k]=(umaxbit[k]==1? (vmax[j]? vmax[j]: j): umaxscope[j])|}$$
+and its dual, where |j=umax[k]|. Those are incorrect when a chain of nodes is
+nested inside a near-set, because the deepest node that is forced into the
+active list at the transition can lie below |vmax[j]| (resp.\ |umax[j]|). The
+smallest example is the five-vertex spider `\.{....++-.+}', whose ten order
+ideals the buggy program lists only eight of, walking off into labelings that
+violate the constraints; on other inputs it loops forever. The correct value of
+|umaxscope[k]| is the largest node still active when spider~$k$ sits at its
+transition labeling with |bit[k]=0|, i.e., when each positive child is at its
+{\it last\/} labeling and each negative child at its {\it first}. We compute it
+with a value-returning analogue of |setfirst|, |setlast|, |setmid|: let
+|firstdeep[k]|, |lastdeep[k]|, |middeep0[k]|, |middeep1[k]| be the largest active
+{\it descendant\/} of~$k$ (or~0 if none) when spider~$k$ holds the labeling that
+|setfirst(k)|, |setlast(k)|, |setmid(k,0)|, |setmid(k,1)| would produce. These
+satisfy one-pass recursions over the children, processed here as $k$ runs from
+$n$ down to~1 so that every child precedes its parent; and
+$|umaxscope[k]|=|middeep0[k]|$ or~$k$, $|vmaxscope[k]|=|middeep1[k]|$ or~$k$.]
 
